decision: changes-requested

The pinned-metadata race is fixed. One fail-open path remains:

- **N52 — high, blocker:** [validate_carry.go:760](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2873662079/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:760) treats a failed blob lookup as absent metadata. Combined with the same assumption at line 713, an unreadable committed metadata blob and an absent working file can discard dependencies and criticality policy, allowing stale results to carry. Establish absence from the committed tree; propagate read failures into full-run fallback. This finding is source-established; scratch creation was denied.
- **N53 — low, follow-up:** [validate.go:1623](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2873662079/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623) still presents carried checks as executed commands in reports. Existing F2.
- **N54 — low, follow-up:** The carried-record seal/verify/closeout fixture remains missing. Existing F1.

Focused CLI and delivery-reader tests, publication/concurrency tests, and `go vet` passed. Artifact-check reported zero errors and 985 warnings. Full validation uses the supplied sealed evidence; persisting assessments were skipped because a scratch copy could not be created. The checkout remains unchanged.

Rules applied: POSE review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style, and delivery evidence. The governance addition maps to D1.

